## Session 3 lab, part B: write your own axioms.
##
## Three small axioms, each practising one idea from the lecture. Write each
## one under its marker, replacing the TODO line. Write Turtle here in any
## text editor, or open this file in Protégé, add the axioms there, and save
## it (File, Save, Turtle). Then run, from demos/session-03-ontology/:
##     python check_my_axioms.py
## The checker runs the HermiT reasoner (about 20 seconds) and says, per
## question, right or not yet, with a hint. Any axiom with the right meaning
## passes, not only one spelling. Only open solutions/my_axioms_solutions.ttl
## after you have tried.
##
## The words you need are all on the lecture slides: owl:disjointWith,
## owl:equivalentClass, owl:intersectionOf, owl:someValuesFrom,
## owl:allValuesFrom. The classes are in scro-extension-reference.ttl.

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ioc:  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/> .
@prefix ul:   <https://ul.edu.lb/kr/scm#> .

<https://ul.edu.lb/kr/my-axioms> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "My Session 3 axioms" ;
    owl:imports <https://ul.edu.lb/kr/scm#> .

ul:LateAtRiskShipment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Late at-risk shipment"@en .

ul:SanctionedOnlyShipment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Sanctioned-only shipment"@en .

